For a particle executing SHM,

$x = A\sin \left(\omega t + ϕ\right) v = \omega A\cos \left(\omega t + ϕ\right) \implies \frac{{v}^{2}}{{\omega }^{2}{A}^{2}} + \frac{{x}^{2}}{{A}^{2}} = 1 \implies$ equation of ellipse between $v$ and $x$

;

The time period of a simple pendulum is given by$T = 2\pi \sqrt{\frac{l}{g}}$

In an upward accelerating frame the effective ${g}_{eff} = g + a \implies {T}_{2} = 2\pi \sqrt{\frac{l}{g + a}} = 2\pi \sqrt{\frac{l}{g + \frac{g}{6}}} \frac{T}{{T}_{2}} = \sqrt{\frac{g + \frac{g}{6}}{g}} = \sqrt{\frac{7}{6}} \implies {T}_{2} = \sqrt{\frac{6}{7}}T$

;
